# {{lb|en|British}} Abbreviation or diminutive for [[baronet]], later replaced by [[Bt]]. It is a post-nominative title; the pre-nominative is Sir (e.g. Sir John Smith Bart.).
#* '''1867''', W.S. Gilbert, ''[[s:The "Bab" Ballads/Joe Golightly|Joe Golightly]]''
#*: The First Lord's daughter proud,
#*: Snubbed earls and viscounts nightly—
#*: She sneered at '''barts''' aloud.
#*: And spurned poor Joe Golightly.

